# ---- LocalCraft standard exclusions (BUILD-STANDARDS §29) ----
# Vercel uploads the repo root (vercel.json pins outputDirectory "."), so
# anything NOT excluded here is served at a guessable URL on the live domain.
#
# ROOT-ANCHORED ON PURPOSE (leading slash). A blanket `*.md` also strips
# content/blog/*.md before the build runs, so the blog renderer builds 0 posts,
# /blog serves an empty index, every post 404s, and the deployment still
# reports READY. That is what happened to Events by Klay.
#
# Internal build + ops docs: LOCALCRAFT-REPO.md names the private GitHub repo,
# the Vercel project and the operator identity; the *-LOG.md files are internal
# build narration, audit scores and known defects.
/*.md

# Installed on Vercel from package.json; never upload the local tree.
node_modules/

# Local `npx serve` preview config; production routing comes from vercel.json.
serve.json

# llms.txt, robots.txt, sitemap.xml, site.webmanifest, favicon.ico and
# og-default.png are deliberately NOT excluded - they are the public surface.
